    "content": "Gerry McNamara is the head coach of the Siena College men's basketball team, leading the Saints to the NCAA Tournament in his second season (2025-26) after a successful 23-11 record and a MAAC Tournament championship. A former Syracuse standout, McNamara previously spent 15 years on the coaching staff at his alma mater. Key Details About Gerry McNamara (Siena Basketball Coach): Hired: 2024-25 season. 2025-26 Season: Led Siena to a 23-11 record, winning the MAAC tournament as a #3 seed and earning a #16 seed in the NCAA tournament (facing Duke). Background: 2003 National Champion at Syracuse. Coaching Style: Highly competitive, focus on fundamentals, and intense, according to players and coaches. Rumors: Amid speculation linking him to the vacant Syracuse head coaching job, McNamara has reiterated his focus on the Siena team, ESPN reported. Other Siena Coaches (As of early 2026): Men's Lacrosse: Tim Cox was named head coach in January 2026, following the passing of former coach Liam Gleason. Baseball: Joe Sheridan is the interim head coach. Note: The primary coaching news in March 2026 surrounds Gerry McNamara's success with the Men's Basketball program.",
